## Findings
1. blocking — brief:99 `[severity: S1]` The acceptance line says each PNG was inspected for clipped controls. But `shots/capture-390-comments.png` (re-opened this round) shows the Capture set dropdown cut off at the right edge: its right border and arrow are missing and there is no margin. Page-level `scrollWidth − clientWidth ≤ 0` (served b3) cannot catch a control clipped inside a container. The required capture evidence is therefore false as stated. Replacement: "Each PNG was inspected for reading order, clipped controls (the 390 Capture set select fits inside the viewport with its right border visible), pin/comment correspondence and plain-English copy; served b3 asserts the select's bounding box lies within the viewport at 390." Fix the select's width at 390 and recapture. `[design: keeps]` [class: review×evidence-backfilled-or-absent] — check: apps/web/tests-serve/w488.spec.ts (none yet: a b3 row asserting `select.boundingBox().x + width ≤ 390`)
2. advisory — brief:19 `[severity: S2]` The text says the packet includes only comments whose "manifest and image still match". But `readUiCaptureComments` (ui-capture-comments.ts:181) compares opus, tree, design digest and manifest hash only, never `imageSha256`. The manifest records name, size and byte count, not a hash, so a same-size image with different bytes keeps the old comment. `review-packet.mjs:431` adds no image check. The same gap is in the reader's list path (serve `read`) and the review path (review-packet); `appendUiCaptureComment` does check the image hash. Replacement: "…includes only comments whose tree, design digest, manifest hash and image hash (`imageSha256` = the set's shot `sha256`) still match." [class: spec×promise-unattainable-under-accepted-domain] — check: none: a b4 fixture with an unchanged manifest and different PNG bytes that expects the comment to be left out
3. advisory — brief:48 `[severity: S3]` "Malformed capture-comment events fail the selected read closed" holds only for lines that parse. A truncated or run-together `ui_capture_comment` line fails `JSON.parse` and is skipped (ui-capture-comments.ts:171-173) before its kind is known. Both readers (serve list and review packet) share this one function. Replacement: "…fail the selected read closed; an unparseable line containing `\"ui_capture_comment\"` is malformed too." [class: review×fail-open-on-malformed-records-patched-per-site] — check: none: a b2 row with a truncated comment line that expects `problems`
4. advisory — brief:74 `[severity: S2]` Author is whatever the client sends under the shared local token: the served row posts both authors with one token, and `appendPatronTimeline`'s role is dropped by `asComment`. A Patron choosing the wrong author goes unnoticed, and the reviewer reads it as attributed. Replacement row text: "…`commentProblem()` rejects every other value; the author is self-declared under the shared local token and is not verified." [class: spec×promise-contract-not-declared] — check: none
5. advisory — brief:17 `[severity: S2]` "Current" means the HEAD tree of whichever checkout `serve` runs from (serve.ts:103-108), and the review packet reads that checkout's `timeline/patron.jsonl`. From the Patron's clone at master, an in-flight opus has no set, and merged sets are all "Older capture" with the form closed. A comment reaches a build review only if `serve` runs on the opus worktree at its certified HEAD. Defaults 1 does not put this to the Patron. Replacement: append to brief:17 "Comments can be placed only while `bisellium serve --studio` runs from the opus worktree at its certified HEAD; a master checkout shows every set as older." Add the same as a limit on brief:52 and brief:58. [class: spec×promise-unattainable-under-accepted-domain] — check: none
6. advisory — brief:52 `[severity: S2]` `readUiCaptureSets` is all-or-nothing (ui-capture-comments.ts:124). One of the real studio's 20 sets with a non-passed `served-e2e`, a missing brief or a bad manifest blanks the whole browser. It also refuses every append (line 195) and every image read (line 257), even for a healthy current set. Replacement limit: "…one unreadable or uncertified set fails the whole listing, every image read and every comment write until it is repaired." [class: spec×promise-unattainable-under-accepted-domain] — check: none: a b1 row with one valid and one failed-gate set, asserting the stated behaviour

